@tradition years-end
// Year's end: day 364, the last evening of the year (a Sunday, Lanterns' last day). The Captain reads a little from the
// year's log in the bow lounge, and the Midtour letters (day 182) come back; the player's comes by Mail. The year's big
// one, so prio 3, like Founding Day. Day 0 (your arrival) is the evening after the year ends, not part of it.
// Design note: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md.
k: 479
title: Year's end
when: year day 364
at: 20:00-21:15
min: 30
prio: 3
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
where: 3 pool mess-seat
hold: none
who: marrow always, oduya always, everyone 80%
anim: officers talk, everyone drink
host: marrow
from: marrow
cake: yes
ties: decor yearsEnd

== mail
- Tomorrow is the year's last evening. Bow lounge, {time}: I'll read a little from the log, and Matthias has your Midtour letters. Come as you are.

== ask
- Year's end tonight. The Captain reads from the log.
- Last night of the year. I want to hear what the Captain reads.   #warm
- Year's end at eight. I hope my letter isn't too silly.   #funny

== here
- Shh. This is the bit about the storm.
- To the Wren, and to another year of her.   #warm
- I'd forgotten half of this. What a year.
- My letter says I'd learn the clarinet. I did not.   #funny

== thanks
- You find a spot in the bow lounge as the Captain reads from the year's log. Some of it is about you.   #warm

== chatter
- The Captain reads at every year's end. Practises for days, you know.   #warm
- Year's end always makes me miss the people who've moved on.   #warm
- I'm keeping my Midtour letter. It's going in the drawer with the others.
